on Herrera, despite scrutiny of his online remarks, an unfiled financial disclosure, and outside groups spending against him. Democrats target the open seat and Polymarket prices the race closer than the lean suggests, but the fundamentals still favor the GOP by a modest margin.", "watch": "Fresh nonpartisan polling or further damage from Herrera's disclosure and remarks controversies could shift this toward a genuine tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Texas's 23rd is an open Republican-held seat after Tony Gonzales's resignation, with a partisan lean of R+7. Gun-rights YouTuber Brandon Herrera leads the Republican side, having raised nearly $2 million, while Democrat Katy Padilla Stout has raised about $485,000 with no outside help so far. Outside groups have spent against Herrera, and headlines flag his online remarks and a still-unfiled financial disclosure.\n\nMost expert raters place the race at Likely Republican, though three call it a Tossup and one Lean Republican, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a four-in-ten chance. The only available poll is a March Democratic-sponsored survey showing a two-point Republican edge. The district's lean keeps the Republican favored, but the open seat, Herrera's controversies, and Democratic targeting make this competitive for the party.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2428, "margin": -4.13}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2506, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.355, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.3283, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.203, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2999, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3496, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2679, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3125, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3009, "margin